# v2.3.0:
[h1]Auto-Build Overhaul:[/h1]
[list]
 [*][b]Auto-Build[/b] has been completely overhauled, split into different smart categories to intelligently handle various constructions.
 [*][b]Custom[/b]: The old auto-build equivalent, with new additions such as capital, market center, control buildings, and more, now with smart logic for prioritizing construction.
 [*][b]Core Goods[/b]: Expands construction material production until prices fall to your target.
 [*][b]Food[/b]: Enables auto-food on the best food locations in markets running short.
 [*][b]Production[/b]: Builds, expands, and upgrades the production buildings and RGOs that pay back fastest.
 [*][b]Roads[/b]: Automatically builds the roads worth the most for Proximity, Market Access, and connecting locations to your capital.
 [*][b]Governors[/b]: Plans and places your governors, founding towns and building roads to prepare them.
[/list]

[h1]New Auto-Close and Auto-Remove Buildings:[/h1]
[list]
 [*]Closes production buildings that have stopped making money and reopens them when their industry recovers.
 [*]Option to destroys them instead where the location has run out of room.
 [*]Customizable based on building profit with optional exceptions for base goods.
[/list]

[h1]New Map Modes:[/h1]
[list]
 [*][b]Recommended Urban Rights[/b] (Economy): Colors each location by the specialization urban right whose buildings can source the most of their input goods from local raw materials.
 [list]
  [*]Hover any location to see every right ranked.
  [*]Grant straight from the map, with right-click also enabling auto-expand for the boosted industries.
  [*]Per-Right Search Filter: Search for the best location for each urban right.
 [/list]
 [*][b]Recommended Governor Placement[/b] and [b]Recommended Capital Location[/b] (Economy): Score every owned location by how much proximity a governor or capital placed there would add.
 [list]
  [*][b]Configurable Scoring[/b]: Rank locations by Proximity, Tax Base, or Population using the new Map Modes tab.
  [*]There is a Recompute Placement Scores button on the action bar to refresh the scores on demand when its open.
 [/list]
 [*][b]Proximity Efficiency Impact[/b] (Geography): Colors locations by how much their terrain affects proximity, natural harbor suitability and maritime presence.
 [*]All map modes can be added to a map section slot, or assigned a keybind.
[/list]

[h1]Auto-Expand Changes:[/h1]
[list]
 [*]Now builds the best candidates first by your chosen metric.
 [*]Now fills all of a location's open construction slots at once, without waiting for the current construction to finish.
 [*]Now supports foreign buildings.
 [*]Ctrl+click now toggles auto-expand for every eligible location in the province.
 [*]Production buildings that are not profitable are not longer expanded unless subsidized under all settings.
 [*]Now only builds where workers will be available within six years, based on current pop growth.
 [*]Workers are now reserved for food production and valuable RGOs (gold, silver, etc.) first.
 [*]ROI in the build location list and production view now counts indirect income (from market access, production efficiency gain, etc).
[/list]

[h1]Auto-Food Changes:[/h1]
[list]
 [*]The Mass Auto-Food tab is gone, replaced by the Auto-Build Food category.
 [*]Now builds when any pops are unemployed instead of waiting for the right worker type.
 [*]Now subsidizes the food buildings it constructs (toggleable).
 [*]The Food Potential map mode now scores every location as if it were rural, and previews when you hover the auto-food toggle.
 [*]The Breadbaskets map mode now includes Auto-Build Food's picks.
 [*]The Upgrade Rank tooltip now shows when a location is locked by Auto-Food.
[/list]

[h1]Urbanization & Urban Rights:[/h1]
[list]
 [*]Auto-Urbanize now has its own tab, toggle, and Min Discount setting.
 [*]New De-Urbanize toggle downgrades location ranks to rural when their RGO is on the Do Not Urbanize list.
 [*]Auto-Grant Urban Rights can now grant each location the specialization right best suited to its local goods, and enable the matching auto-expands.
 [*]The build location list now shows each location's granted or recommended urban rights.
[/list]

[h1]New Filters:[/h1]
[list]
 [*][b]Local Access to Raw Materials Bonus[/b]: Shows the production bonus a building gets when its input goods are produced by RGOs in the province.
 [*][b]Owned Locations[/b]: Show buildings in locations you own.
 [*][b]Administrator[/b]: Shows characters with the Administrator cabinet trait.
 [*]Tax Base and Wealth filters now treat their maximum as no upper limit (100+).
[/list]

[h1]Settings Menu Overhaul:[/h1]
[list]
 [*]The settings window is reorganized into tabs with sub-tabs per feature.
 [*]Some settings have now been integrated into their vanilla equivalents, and can be controlled in the vanilla automation panel as well as the dedicated menu.
 [*]Auto-expand of buildings, RGOs, and food is now enabled by default, and Auto-Upgrade All Buildings moved lower in the priority order.
[/list]

[h1]Performance:[/h1]
[list]
 [*]Performance is much improved across the whole mod.
 [*]Large countries now spread automation work across months instead of processing everything at once.
 [*]More information is cached so loading a initialized save game should have no performance impact.
 [*]The Food Potential map mode is far faster now.
[/list]

[h1]Fixes:[/h1]
[list]
 [*]Fix the Remove Urban Rights Costs setting not removing the manual grant and revoke costs.
 [*]Fix a location keeping Auto-Food's rank lock when an event upgrades its rank anyway.
 [*]Fix shortage prevention in multiplayer not counting what other players were already building in the same market.
 [*]Improved various tooltips & headers, fixing outdated ones, and making other ones more clear.
[/list]

# v2.2.12:
- Fix the vanilla Auto-Expand Buildings and Auto-Expand R.G.O. automations staying on in the background if you had them enabled before installing the mod, with no way to turn them back off

# v2.2.11:
- Permanent fix for auto-expand failing sometimes in large nations (more performative, and catches more/all edge cases now)

# v2.2.10:
- Update some outdated tooltips
- Add back revoke cost to Urban Rights (leftover removal I forgot about from testing, can still be turned off using the Remove Urban Rights Costs setting).

# v2.2.9:
- Shortage-Prevention: Auto-construction now skips builds that would cause a construction goods shortage in the local market
- Fix auto-expand not building anything in large nations
- The building auto-expand tooltip now explains that base good buildings are expanded regardless of profitability

# v2.2.8:
- Fix RGO auto-expand not reserving gold already committed to other builds in the same cycle, so it could spend below your gold reserve
- Fix error log spam from Auto-Urbanize

# v2.2.7:
- Auto-Expand, Auto-Build, and Auto-Food now build in locations where the workers will fill the new job through promotion within a year, instead of needing enough free pops right away
- Make the building classification map firing more robust which should resolve the issues some people are facing of incorrect metrics (missing pops/gold)
- Adding some missing conditions to the RGO auto-expand tooltip

# v2.2.6:
- Update for game v1.3.6
- Fix the mass auto-expand button showing on foreign-owned buildings

# v2.2.5:
- Fix production efficiency, enhancement production efficiency, and ROI overflowing in the production view when all three are shown at once

# v2.2.4:
- Update auto-expand buttons for buildings in the per-location view.
- Make mass auto-expand button appear for buildings that you don't have a level for yet in the macro builder.

# v2.2.3:
- The Food Potential Per RGO Level mapmode now opens automatically when you open the food production view
- Update Glorp UI integration
- Fix the Auto-Expand threshold formatting not reverting after switching the metric from ROI back to Tax Income or Profit
- Fix the Auto-Expand Metric not working for buildings

# v2.2.2:
- Added vanilla government power cost for Auto-Grant Urban Rights
- Add a Minimum Government Power setting that stops auto-granting before your government power drops below it, you can also enable unrestricted tools in CMF settings->Remove Government Power Cost to disable it (mainly for my own testing)
- Auto-Food and the Auto-Urbanize ignore list now hides RGO's you don't have
- Auto-Expand RGO is now disabled in locations where Auto-Food is active (redundant)
- Fix the settings "reset to default" button not restoring the correct starting values for some lists
- Fix Auto-Urbanize queuing a duplicate rank upgrade while one is already under construction
- Fix mass-mode Auto-Food locations not showing in the Breadbaskets mapmode
- Fix the Auto-Expand Metric sometimes not applying correctly after switching it
- The auto-expand tooltip now shows when the building auto-expand feature is turned off
- Reworked construction queuing to run more reliably

# v2.2.1:
- Fix broken translations
- Fix edge case where auto-expand and auto-upgrade, both queuing at the same exact time, constructing two levels instead of 1.

# v2.2.0:
- Complete core logic overhaul: construction decisions now use the game's real cost and income numbers instead of the mod's own estimates
- New Auto-Expand Metric setting: gate auto-expand of buildings and RGOs on Tax Income, Profit, ROI (Tax), or ROI (Profit)
- Auto-expand selections now automatically transfer to the replacement building type when the original becomes obsolete
- Auto-expand buttons are now hidden on obsolete buildings
- Ported building view UI changes from Glorp UI (so I don't have to duplicate work)
- The production view now shows Return on Investment (also added to Glorp UI)
- Auto-expand tooltips now show the actual construction cost and how much gold you need before the expand will queue
- More accurate cost and income estimates for RGO auto-expand
- Added 7 more urban rights to the Auto-Grant Urban Rights list
- The Found Town and Found City buildings now cost approximately the same as upgrading the location rank directly
- Reorganized the settings window
- Removed wool from Auto-Food since wool no longer produces food
- Fix buildings that cost religious influence or other special currencies being built without paying
- Fix auto-upgrade queueing duplicate upgrades for buildings already being upgraded (could construct extra levels)
- Fix the auto-expand button showing on foreign-owned buildings in the build menu
- Fix the auto-expand button and icon sometimes not appearing
- Fix more error log spam


# v2.1.3:
- Fix one broken icon
- Fix error log spam

# v2.1.2:
- Redid 1.3 integration (this time less rushed) with the mod more naturally integrating into the vanilla UI
- Auto-Urbanize will no longer urbanize locations where Mass Auto-Food is enabled.

# v2.1.1:
- Many fixes for v1.3

# v2.1.0:
- Updated for EU5 v1.3 "Pavia"
- Auto-expand buttons now use the game's new built-in auto-expand icon and checkbox
- Integrated with the game's Automation panel: its "Auto-Expand Buildings" and "Auto-Expand R.G.O." entries now stay in sync with Construction Manager's on/off, and their button opens the Construction Manager settings instead of the production view

# v2.0.2:
- Fix some broken non-english localizations
- Prevent auto-build from queueing up building levels beyond the cap
- Prevent auto-upgrade from queueing upgrades for in-progress buildings

# v2.0.1:
- Change max gold reserve to 100k
- Change default min discount to 0%
- Correct some localizations
- Prevent granting town rights where the requirements aren't met
- Correct min profit (was checking the profit of all levels, rather than per level); it does not apply until a building has a level constructed

# v2.0.0:
[h1]New Automation:[/h1]
[list]
 [*][b]Auto-Upgrade All Buildings[/b]: Upgrades obsolete buildings to their next tier across your country, regardless of whether auto-expand is on for that building.
 [*][b]Auto-Food[/b]: Builds food-producing RGOs and food buildings in rural locations, picking the highest marginal food output. Can be enabled on a per location, or through a mass toggle based on your selected criteria (i.e. wheat on a river).
 [*][b]Auto-Urbanize[/b]: Promotes rural settlements to towns and towns to cities each month. Sub-toggles per tier, plus an RGO ignore list (gold, gems, spices, etc.).
 [*][b]Auto-Build Capital[/b]: Constructs your capital-only buildings (royal court, supreme court, war college, admiralty, chancery, parliament, etc.) when conditions allow.
 [*][b]Auto-Grant Urban Rights[/b]: Grants enabled urban rights to your cities and megalopolises in priority order.
[/list]

[h1]New Filters:[/h1]
[list]
 [*]Tax Base and Wealth (with and without control scaling)
 [*]Building Levels Filled (relative to supported cap)
 [*]Production Efficiency and Building Level
 [*]Food Potential Per RGO Level
 [*]R.G.O. Value
 [*]Number of Locations Per Province
 [*]Attacker Penalty (from terrain)
 [*]Good Migration Candidate (non-city under 30k pops)
[/list]

[h1]New Mapmodes:[/h1]
[list]
 [*][b]Breadbaskets[/b]: Highlights locations where auto-food is enabled.
 [*][b]Food Potential Per RGO Level[/b]: Colors locations by natural food potential. Factors in rgo, terrain, vegetation, climate, named static modifiers, water access, and assumed-max bonuses from windmill, farming village, and irrigation systems etc.
[/list]

[h1]New Integration:[/h1]
[list]
 [*]Integrates with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3601047146]Glorp UI[/url] - Load Glorp UI after/below Construction Manager
 [*]Integrated with the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3692202776]Community Mod Framework[/url]
[/list]

[h1]New Requirements:[/h1]
Now requires the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3692202776]Community Mod Framework[/url].
